Date: 2026-09-10
Subject: [PATCH] fix(charxiv): cast prediction to string before replacement

CharXiv scoring builds a grading prompt with:

    line["grading_query"].replace("{PREDICTION}", line["prediction"])

Some model predictions are stored as numeric values (or NaN). Python then
raises:

    TypeError: replace() argument 2 must be str, not float

Cast the prediction through str() before replacement so the judge can score
already-generated predictions without rerunning inference.

Applied to VLMEvalKit commit ce95c4d14829b8ed688fdfaea210c4bb510e1a35.
---
 vlmeval/dataset/charxiv.py | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/vlmeval/dataset/charxiv.py b/vlmeval/dataset/charxiv.py
index 0000000..0000000 100644
--- a/vlmeval/dataset/charxiv.py
+++ b/vlmeval/dataset/charxiv.py
@@ -25,7 +25,7 @@ def auxeval(judge_model: Any, line: pd.Series, **kwargs: Any) -> Dict[str, Any]:
     Returns:
         Dict containing evaluation results with extract_answer and score
     """
     failure_result = {"extracted_answer": "Failed to parse response", "score": 0.0}
-    prompt = line["grading_query"].replace("{PREDICTION}", line["prediction"])
+    prompt = line["grading_query"].replace("{PREDICTION}", str(line["prediction"]))
 
     retry = kwargs.get("retry", 10)
 
